Z||000000||Leroy Brown||09-02-2000||03:00 PM||||Can the long block from a car other than a fiero be used with the Fiero accessories?<BR>My 2.8 is very tired but can not find any used Fiero 2.8 but cavaliers etc are. Are the<BR>internals different? Block? etc.<BR>Help<BR>Thanks<BR>Leroy||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||09-02-2000||09:40 PM||||I think the Cavalier 2.8 will fit. You will want to keep your Fiero plenum, throttle body, sensors and etc. I believe the Cavalier had a different EFI setup. Also, the heads might have smaller valves, and the cam might be milder. <P>I could be wrong about any of the above. I hope someone will call me on it if I am. Merely offering items to consider...<P>This is, however, a good question. <BR>Maybe my post will help keep it up toward the top, where it will receive an "educated" response.<P>BTW... Welcome to the Forum! I have never seen such a large assemblage of Fiero knowledge, anywhere else.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-02-2000||11:24 PM||||Try something aroud '88 or so Jimmy or Blazer. As far as I know they are the same, other than that you need a 'W' block and start from the block up, or do a total rebuild on yours.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-03-2000||10:51 AM||||I have an 88 2.8-liter short block for sale with 50,000 miles. I am selling it because I am replacing it with a 3.4-liter Camaro engine. You can purchase it from Kick Hill farm @ <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/bodypart.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kickhill.com/bodypart.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-03-2000||03:06 PM||||Doesn't the Jimmy/Blazer 2.8 have the starter on the wrong side? It would almost have to be a FWD 2.8.||||reg||1
